@startuml
left to right direction

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus Study Room Booking System" {

  usecase "Book a free study room" as UC1
  usecase "View room availability" as UC2
  usecase "Cancel own booking" as UC3

  usecase "Block a room" as UC4
  usecase "Unblock a room" as UC5
  usecase "Review room usage" as UC6

  usecase "Receive booking confirmation" as UC7

  Student --> UC1
  Student --> UC2
  Student --> UC3

  Administrator --> UC4
  Administrator --> UC5
  Administrator --> UC6

  UC1 ..> UC7 : <<include>>
}

note right of UC1
  Constraints:
  R1: Future start, duration > 0
      and <= 2 hours
  R2: No overlapping active
      bookings for the same room
  R3: Blocked rooms cannot
      accept new bookings
end note

note right of UC3
  R2 applies to the booking
  being released.
end note

note bottom of UC4
  R3: Blocking a room prevents
  new bookings.
end note

note bottom of UC5
  R3: Unblocking makes the room
  available for new bookings.
end note

note bottom
  Assumptions:
  1. "Book a free study room" includes
     checking that the requested slot
     satisfies R1-R3.
  2. A booking confirmation is produced
     only after a booking succeeds.
  3. Students may cancel only their own
     bookings.
  4. Room usage review is an
     administrator-only goal.
  5. No separate use cases are modeled
     for payments, equipment, recurring
     bookings, waiting lists, extra
     notifications, or registration.
end note

@enduml